# Nothing writes a certificate or a key into this directory any more — both halves live in this user's own data
# directory, outside the repository, so that a container mounted on the same workspace cannot overwrite the
# host's pair. See paths.mjs.
#
# These names stay ignored anyway, for the checkouts that ran an older generator and still have the files
# sitting here. Dropping the root's three lines once already cost a leaked private key: a stale pair that was no
# longer ignored got swept into a commit and pushed. The rule costs nothing and is the only thing standing
# between a leftover file and that happening again.
localhost.crt
localhost.key
localhost-com-ca.crt
localhost-com-ca.key
localhost-com-ca.srl
